1
00:00:00,867 --> 00:00:04,904
Your project lives in files: the PRD, the architecture,

2
00:00:04,904 --> 00:00:09,007
epics, stories and sprint status, spread across folders.

3
00:00:09,767 --> 00:00:12,874
Agile Project UI brings them together in one view,

4
00:00:12,874 --> 00:00:14,427
right in your browser.

5
00:00:16,567 --> 00:00:20,275
It's a local-first web app, compatible with BMAD Method,

6
00:00:20,275 --> 00:00:22,967
to read, edit and discuss your project.

7
00:00:23,700 --> 00:00:25,748
No accounts and no database:

8
00:00:25,748 --> 00:00:28,820
your files remain the single source of truth.

9
00:00:32,567 --> 00:00:35,241
I start by choosing the project folder.

10
00:00:35,241 --> 00:00:37,676
Chrome or Edge asks for permission,

11
00:00:37,676 --> 00:00:40,647
and the app reads the files on your machine.

12
00:00:41,400 --> 00:00:43,471
It detects the BMAD version,

13
00:00:43,471 --> 00:00:46,213
loads every document and opens the PRD.

14
00:00:46,213 --> 00:00:49,320
For now it's read mode: nothing gets changed.

15
00:00:52,500 --> 00:00:55,266
On the left you get the whole project tree,

16
00:00:55,266 --> 00:00:57,580
with a search box to find any file.

17
00:00:58,600 --> 00:01:02,397
Markdown reads like a real document: headings,

18
00:01:02,397 --> 00:01:06,120
tables and an outline to jump to any section.

19
00:01:06,900 --> 00:01:09,786
Relative links open the linked document,

20
00:01:09,786 --> 00:01:13,300
and local images load without leaving your folder.

21
00:01:16,467 --> 00:01:19,066
The stories tab shows them by status,

22
00:01:19,066 --> 00:01:21,907
exactly as they're written in your files.

23
00:01:22,800 --> 00:01:26,554
I can filter by epic and open a card: description,

24
00:01:26,554 --> 00:01:30,240
tasks, and the file and line behind every detail.

25
00:01:31,000 --> 00:01:34,006
If a status isn't recognised, it's never guessed:

26
00:01:34,006 --> 00:01:36,520
it's set apart, with its original value.

27
00:01:37,267 --> 00:01:40,121
Epics group their stories with expandable tasks,

28
00:01:40,121 --> 00:01:43,187
and the sprint view sums up how everything is going.

29
00:01:45,800 --> 00:01:47,068
For extra detail,

30
00:01:47,068 --> 00:01:50,432
there's a catalogue of installed agents and a diagnosis

31
00:01:50,432 --> 00:01:51,700
of what was read.

32
00:01:54,900 --> 00:01:57,676
To change something, I turn on edit mode.

33
00:01:57,676 --> 00:02:01,220
The browser asks for write access to this folder only.

34
00:02:01,967 --> 00:02:05,713
Now I drag a story that was ready to start into the In

35
00:02:05,713 --> 00:02:07,087
progress column.

36
00:02:07,833 --> 00:02:10,790
Before saving, I see exactly what changes:

37
00:02:10,790 --> 00:02:13,993
the story and the sprint status, file by file.

38
00:02:15,167 --> 00:02:16,100
I confirm,

39
00:02:16,100 --> 00:02:19,541
and the app writes the files and checks the result is

40
00:02:19,541 --> 00:02:21,407
exactly what was expected.

41
00:02:22,133 --> 00:02:24,064
Documents are editable too,

42
00:02:24,064 --> 00:02:26,989
right on the text or in the Markdown source.

43
00:02:26,989 --> 00:02:29,973
I'll add an action item to the meeting notes.

44
00:02:31,800 --> 00:02:33,698
I review the change and save.

45
00:02:33,698 --> 00:02:35,975
If someone edits the file elsewhere,

46
00:02:35,975 --> 00:02:38,360
your draft is kept so you can compare.

47
00:02:41,533 --> 00:02:43,993
To discuss, I open the comments panel.

48
00:02:43,993 --> 00:02:46,733
Sam already left a question on these notes.

49
00:02:47,500 --> 00:02:50,116
I reply that yes, with a return date,

50
00:02:50,116 --> 00:02:53,340
and leave a reaction so Sam knows I've read it.

51
00:02:54,367 --> 00:02:56,704
I can also start a new thread:

52
00:02:56,704 --> 00:02:58,975
I select any passage of text,

53
00:02:58,975 --> 00:03:01,247
write my comment and save it.

54
00:03:03,233 --> 00:03:04,968
Threads can be resolved,

55
00:03:04,968 --> 00:03:08,092
and they're saved as files next to your project,

56
00:03:08,092 --> 00:03:10,753
outside BMAD's output and ready for Git.

57
00:03:11,500 --> 00:03:15,603
Prefer working in the dark? Light, dark or system theme,

58
00:03:15,603 --> 00:03:16,860
in one click.

59
00:03:20,067 --> 00:03:23,099
When you're ready to share, the Git connector steps in:

60
00:03:23,099 --> 00:03:26,627
an optional program that runs on your computer with your own Git.

61
00:03:27,767 --> 00:03:30,668
The guide gives you the commands for your system.

62
00:03:30,668 --> 00:03:33,779
I connect it with its session key and confirm I trust

63
00:03:33,779 --> 00:03:34,887
the repository.

64
00:03:35,633 --> 00:03:38,205
Now I can see the branch and local changes.

65
00:03:38,205 --> 00:03:40,042
I pick just the files I want,

66
00:03:40,042 --> 00:03:43,033
write a message and review the commit with the real

67
00:03:43,033 --> 00:03:44,713
diff before confirming it.

68
00:03:46,767 --> 00:03:50,389
Push is a separate step: I see every outgoing commit,

69
00:03:50,389 --> 00:03:51,556
then confirm.

70
00:03:51,556 --> 00:03:54,687
Nothing leaves your machine until you decide.

71
00:03:57,867 --> 00:04:00,030
If your team uses Jira or Confluence,

72
00:04:00,030 --> 00:04:03,049
there are separate connectors you set up step by step:

73
00:04:03,049 --> 00:04:05,112
the local address, the session key,

74
00:04:05,112 --> 00:04:07,627
the project and a final check before saving.

75
00:04:10,967 --> 00:04:12,687
I link a story to its issue,

76
00:04:12,687 --> 00:04:14,509
compare the fields three ways,

77
00:04:14,509 --> 00:04:16,887
and review any import before applying it.

78
00:04:21,033 --> 00:04:23,464
Your documents never leave your computer:

79
00:04:23,464 --> 00:04:26,154
the server only delivers the app. No accounts,

80
00:04:26,154 --> 00:04:27,033
no syncing.

81
00:04:28,733 --> 00:04:30,129
To get started,

82
00:04:30,129 --> 00:04:34,250
open the web app in Chrome or Edge and pick your folder.

83
00:04:34,250 --> 00:04:37,773
For development: clone, npm ci and npm run dev.

84
00:04:38,533 --> 00:04:42,053
Agile Project UI. Your project, from its files.
